-libstb Python API
-=================
-
-**libstb** gives Python the `stb <https://github.com/nothings/stb>`_ single-header
-libraries through a nanobind extension: image decoding and encoding (PNG, JPEG, BMP,
-TGA), resizing with selectable filters, image editing, EXIF orientation, TrueType
-font rendering and zlib streams. There are no system dependencies and no Python dependencies; numpy and
-Pillow are optional.
-
-.. code-block:: python
-
-   import libstb as stb
-
-   img = stb.Image.open("photo.png")
-   small = img.resize(320, 240, "cubic")
-   small.write("photo.jpg")               # format from the extension
-
-   pixels = stb.imread("photo.png")       # ndarray, needs numpy
-
-Installation
-------------
-
-.. code-block:: bash
-
-   pip install libstb
-
-.. toctree::
-   :maxdepth: 1
-
-   Overview <self>
-   image
-   resizer
-   font
-   zlib
-   simd
-   threads
-   errors
